Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:50:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.04 Linux update helper

Adds linux-only phlink_update_helper executable and apply logic:

  phlink_update_helper --apply <staging_dir> <target_path>
                                <signature_path> <gpg_keyring>

Pipeline:
  1. Read staged.json (StagedPayload v1).
  2. Confirm payload exists.
  3. gpg --batch --no-default-keyring --keyring <keyring> --verify
     against the bundled phlink release public key.
  4. base::Move (rename(2)) the verified payload over the target.
  5. Delete staged.json.

Same exit-code surface as macOS helper. Tests cover argument
validation, missing-staged.json, and a happy-path replacement (gpg
verification skipped via test-only ApplyOptions::skip_signature_check).

Build target is gated on is_linux; mac compiles only the GN graph.
The signed-payload path will be exercised in CI on the linux nightly
build (deferred to 10-08).

Refs phlink phase 10-04.
